} "Rapid-Fire Pistol, 25 metres, Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "4 –  5 August 2024"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2189"} "National Shooting Centre, Châteauroux, France"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/2013103"} "29 from 19 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/133197"} "Li Yuehong"] " had been a contender for medals at major championships for over a decade, but in 2023 and 2024 he had hit a purple patch in his career. He had won three gold medals at the 2023 World Championships, with an especially dominant performance in rapid fire pistol, highlighted by a world record score in the final. His main rivals should have been the representatives of the host country, reigning champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/133905"} "Jean Quiquampoix"] " and two-time World silver medalist " [:a {:href "/athletes/142912"} "Clément Bessaguet"] ", but they failed to live up to their reputations, with Quiquampoix finishing well down the field and Bessaguet being eliminated early in the final."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Li Yuehong led the qualifiers for the final, and was in gold medal position until surprisingly overtaken by Korean soldier " [:a {:href "/athletes/154184"} "Jo Yeong-Jae"] " at the halfway point. The final three series of shots were a triumph for Li and disappointing for Jo, as the Chinese marksman exerted his superiority to claim the Olympic championships. Jo held on for silver, with Li’s Chinese compatriot " [:a {:href "/athletes/154096"} "Wang Xinjie"] " adding to China’s medal haul with the bronze medal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Bib"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1162"] [:td {}